    title: "SHIF in Kenya 2026: Rates, PAYE Treatment and SHA",
    slug: "understanding-shif-deductions-in-kenya-and-what-replaced-nhif",
    metaTitle: "SHIF Deductions Kenya: NHIF Replacement Guide",
    metaDescription: "How SHIF replaced NHIF in Kenya, how salary contributions are calculated, why SHIF is deductible for PAYE and how to verify payments with SHA.",
    content: "<h2>SHIF in Kenya: what replaced NHIF?</h2><p>Kenya's Social Health Authority (SHA) started operating the Social Health Insurance Fund (SHIF) in October 2024. SHIF replaced the old NHIF contribution arrangements. Historical NHIF graduated contribution tables should not be used to work out present-day SHIF charges.</p><h2>How salary contributions work</h2><p>For salaried employees, SHIF is generally assessed at 2.75% of gross salary. For example, an employee whose gross pay is KSh 50,000 would ordinarily have a KSh 1,375 SHIF payroll deduction before any personal circumstances or assessment differences. Check your registration and any household contribution assessment on the official SHA portal.</p><h2>How SHIF affects PAYE</h2><p>Contributions made to SHIF have been deductible in determining taxable employment income under the Tax Laws (Amendment) Act 2024, for December 2024 and later payroll. SHIF is not an extra 15% insurance-relief credit: the distinction between a deduction from taxable income and a reduction in final tax is important.</p><h2>Employer remittance and records</h2><p>Employers should use the official SHA Employer Portal to assess and remit contributions. SHA's employer notice calls for remittance by the ninth day of each month. Employees should reconcile the SHIF deduction shown on their payslip with the relevant SHA membership and payment record.</p><h2>What to do if your SHIF payment is missing</h2><p>First ask payroll for the remittance reference and contribution period, then check the official SHA account. Do not send personal information or contributions to unverified numbers circulating online. The official employer portal is <a href=\"https://employers.sha.go.ke/\">employers.sha.go.ke</a>.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Does NHIF still use its old salary bands?</h3><p>No. Those bands were replaced by SHIF arrangements from October 2024.</p><h3>Is SHIF deducted before PAYE?</h3><p>KRA lists SHIF contributions among deductible items in determining taxable employment income.</p><p>Official references: <a href=\"https://www.kra.go.ke/individual/filing-paying/types-of-taxes/paye\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">KRA PAYE</a>, <a href=\"https://www.kra.go.ke/news-center/public-notices/2157-amendments-to-paye-computation-pursuant-to-the-tax-laws-amendment-act%2C-2024\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">KRA PAYE amendments</a>, <a href=\"https://www.nssf.or.ke/notice-to-employers-year-4-2026-nssf-contribution-rates\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">NSSF 2026 notice</a> and <a href=\"https://employers.sha.go.ke/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">SHA employer portal</a>. Reviewed 22 October 2026.</p>",
