    metaDescription: "The employer's cost is greater than take-home pay and may exceed the contractual gross salary.",
    lastReviewedAt: "2026-10-22",
    content: "<p><strong>Editorial review: 22 October 2026.</strong> The employer's cost is greater than take-home pay and may exceed the contractual gross salary.</p><h2>How it works</h2><p>Separate gross salary, employer NSSF, employer housing levy, leave, insurance and operating overheads rather than treating all statutory charges as one payroll deduction.</p><h2>What to verify before acting</h2><p>Cost also varies with employment terms, benefits and the wage base used for contributions.</p><h2>Practical checks</h2><ol><li>Identify the service, tax year or transaction type that applies to your situation.</li><li>Check the latest applicable legal or provider information rather than an undated fee table.</li><li>Keep the official calculation, payment reference, policy or account documents.</li><li>Ask the responsible employer, institution or regulator to explain any discrepancy.</li></ol><h2>Related guidance</h2><p>For tax and payroll questions, use the <a href=\"/blog/how-to-calculate-your-paye-tax-in-kenya/\">KRA PAYE guide</a> and our <a href=\"/blog/the-complete-guide-to-nssf-contributions-in-kenya/\">2026 NSSF guide</a>. For payments, check the relevant official provider's current tariff or instructions before sending.</p><p><em>This guide provides general information, not a personalised tax assessment, financial recommendation or confirmed payment quote. Last reviewed 22 October 2026.</em></p>",
