    metaTitle: "File PAYE Returns on iTax Kenya Penalty-Free",
    metaDescription: "Employer guide to monthly KRA PAYE iTax filings, due on the ninth day of the following month, with nil returns, deductions and common errors.",
    content: "<h2>Filing monthly PAYE through KRA iTax</h2><p>Employers are responsible for accounting for payroll PAYE and filing the monthly return with the Kenya Revenue Authority. The general due date is <strong>the ninth day of the following month</strong>, including the corresponding tax remittance.</p><h2>Before submitting</h2><ol><li>Reconcile all taxable pay and non-cash benefits for the relevant month.</li><li>Check employee NSSF, SHIF and Affordable Housing Levy details and allowable deductions.</li><li>Confirm resident and non-resident tax treatment and relief entitlement.</li><li>Compute PAYE using the published monthly KRA progressive bands.</li><li>Log into <a href=\"https://itax.kra.go.ke/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">KRA iTax</a>, select the relevant return, upload or complete the current schedule and verify the totals.</li><li>Generate the payment registration number and use the payment method shown by KRA.</li></ol><h2>Is a nil PAYE return required?</h2><p>KRA states that a nil return should be submitted if no PAYE is to be declared and an active PAYE filing obligation applies. Do not assume zero deductions mean the return may be ignored.</p><h2>Common employer errors</h2><p>Using old NHIF tables instead of SHIF, outdated NSSF contribution ceilings, the wrong PAYE month, or treating employer contributions as employee salary deductions can make a filed return inaccurate. Review the <a href=\"/blog/how-to-calculate-your-paye-tax-in-kenya/\">PAYE calculation</a> and <a href=\"/blog/the-complete-guide-to-nssf-contributions-in-kenya/\">NSSF</a> guides first.</p><h2>Late filing and payment</h2><p>KRA publishes specific penalties for late PAYE returns and late payment. The precise consequences depend on the obligation and amounts; confirm your actual position through iTax or KRA support before making a settlement.</p><p>Source: <a href=\"https://www.kra.go.ke/individual/filing-paying/types-of-taxes/paye\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">KRA PAYE guide</a>.</p><p><em>Reviewed 22 October 2026. Compliance rules and online procedures can change. Rely on the official KRA iTax portal for amounts due and statutory filing requirements.</em></p>",
